            <div xml:id="m-2652fa3b-ca0b-46a5-96a6-9113e6fdac7b">
              <lg xml:id="m-c64c9bd5-8c42-4098-b4ee-e792581e3bbb">
                <l xml:id="m-432a3a7f-1ee0-485d-a87b-0d13e4334727" facs="#m-6bab7efa-fb0a-49c1-93cc-b3c92484d4f0" label="text-like">sunday within the octave of Christmas.</l><l xml:id="m-5081ae3f-9234-4b8f-8629-5d1ba679b393" facs="#m-c3cff76d-b933-4785-85e2-becbe30d3b25" label="ambiguous">433</l><l xml:id="m-04545ef1-4e35-466b-a3d1-a8e98150bd69" facs="#m-77f171ad-2b1b-4a37-9f14-4e4999f5241a" label="text-like">Sunday within the Octave of Christmas.</l><l xml:id="m-66fd3701-c03e-4d82-8a48-acfdff8f812b" facs="#m-d583abe8-2de3-4876-9fa9-3dcecb927d6d" label="text-like">If the Feast of St. Thomas or of St. Silvester falls on a Sunday, the Office</l><l xml:id="m-386fa783-890b-4309-b1a7-0c80bdf3d5a6" facs="#m-7211d2f0-f502-4875-8f7c-b551a7cc3ad3" label="text-like">is of the Sunday with a commemoration of the occurring Feast and of the</l><l xml:id="m-3be97353-c681-4705-b8fa-2ee4a025ea2d" facs="#m-cea4339b-2939-4100-99ef-3ebb266562df" label="text-like">Octave of the Nativity.</l><l xml:id="m-9a8df72a-4b7e-4701-b521-b81a1800e263" facs="#m-f175217c-2da9-44a9-864a-db67a9d113e6" label="text-like">In England, however, if the Feast of St. Thomas falls on a Sundar, the</l><l xml:id="m-b6dd1da5-cc21-438f-8399-1d6c9a02aa5a" facs="#m-d1d1d118-e0e5-491e-903a-b992fab7b64d" label="lyrics-like">Ofice is of the Feast with commemorations of the Sunday and of the Ôctave</l><l xml:id="m-33581cc0-2967-45c9-81ce-e7dfb98b79a2" facs="#m-5e99a36a-f3fb-481c-9bb1-e0cd454ee7c6" label="text-like">of the Nativity.</l><l xml:id="m-ceeb8675-6519-4726-85a9-05f1628518cb" facs="#m-a30215f4-808c-49a2-ba50-a71e9a6fe7a7" label="text-like">AT FIRST VESPERS.</l><l xml:id="m-2933045f-f4f3-4dfa-85e4-31008ec1aba8" facs="#m-164462bb-907b-4bad-886d-d3fb1927a97d" label="text-like">Antiphons and Psalms ofthe Nativity, p. 411; the Antiphons are not doubled.</l><l xml:id="m-2e45d2f0-91d1-4dbc-bac8-5ddbfdd3128e" facs="#m-90345ac3-18e0-4161-95a6-cb9be4e9cce1" label="lyrics-like">Chapter. Fratres: Quanto témpore. p. 437. — Hymn. Jésu Redém¬</l><l xml:id="m-737953de-4beb-4130-8ecb-548aa4b8430b" facs="#m-cd72a711-3880-472e-a824-308460a22dd2" label="ambiguous">ptor. p. 365.</l><l xml:id="m-7e241969-9c27-4513-b7ec-b6ea81b2d921" facs="#m-2bd8dc03-f20c-46c7-baac-3819a49abea8" label="lyrics-like">V. Vérbum cáro fáctum est, allelúia. B. Et habitávit in nóbis, allelúia.</l><l xml:id="m-bf87d777-df27-4645-86ed-fe57f7832f22" facs="#m-356abbc8-04b4-4b4e-a2fd-4d67f7bb19ca" label="text-like">At Magn.</l><l xml:id="m-a9f62f61-86d1-4eba-86f5-9b05942f3562" facs="#m-4f9ae567-d87d-4be1-9603-4744b6921f2e" label="ambiguous">Ant. S. G</l><l xml:id="m-2489295a-faae-4c6a-b87f-4b8b7256130b" facs="#m-d18a7301-bb7c-4709-9deb-40f0e3c4cbeb" label="lyrics-like">DUM mé-di-um si-lénti-um“ tené-rent ómni¬</l><l xml:id="m-2b056b23-a9cf-4110-af6a-6a5149850655" facs="#m-77a200d2-776a-4b99-b9e6-1f0540b0b036" label="lyrics-like">à, et nox in sú-o cúrsu médi-um (ter per-áge-ret : omní¬</l><l xml:id="m-e0157aaa-4d5b-4f73-9f93-5fc69b20bbf5" facs="#m-0a84a9cc-940c-44da-9cb8-18f034a4ba5c" label="lyrics-like">a regá-li-bus sédibus vé nit,</l><l xml:id="m-788b9dee-a7b2-46af-a8e6-1168fac3c912" facs="#m-0cc22c3d-50a3-453a-afc2-ec3e843ec5e7" label="lyrics-like">pot-ens sérmo tú-us Dómine</l><l xml:id="m-7b005b9d-a331-463d-9668-054b96a3af48" facs="#m-b00d36bb-87c0-4e73-9a15-4b307a9e16e4" label="lyrics-like">alle-lú-ia. E u o u a e.</l><l xml:id="m-9d290cc8-a35e-47c3-ab4f-7a6670d0b1f9" facs="#m-5d9b6914-2ff6-414e-b05f-7f53cf8a8483" label="lyrics-like">Cant. Magníficat. 8. G. p. 212.— Prayer. Omnípotens sempitérne. D. 434.</l><l xml:id="m-ac45565c-382e-43c2-9c80-ed5447a1b22b" facs="#m-e9bf0ddf-266d-4539-8bf4-4a1c19cf8a36" label="lyrics-like">Commemoration is then made of the Nativity (Ant. Hódie. p. 418. Y. Nótum.</l><l xml:id="m-e3e1de57-262e-42bb-ac3e-70f1ab5c7550" facs="#m-53e5db55-f820-4a3c-97a9-89d0f3b8f512" label="lyrics-like">Prayer. Concéde); but on Dec. "oth a Commemoration is first' made ot</l><l xml:id="m-85bcadcf-4193-47a2-8efc-5c8da7239778" facs="#m-2e4bd6f6-6b9b-41cb-b1e0-e7e26416f620" label="text-like">St. Thomas. On Dec. Joth, commemoration is made of the Nativity, then or</l><l xml:id="m-f257642d-4003-4925-acd6-cf7fe59bbffc" facs="#m-ed1850f0-b2b5-415f-a8a2-9772ee0c6b61" label="ambiguous">St. Silvester.</l><l xml:id="m-2c027c8c-6bae-488c-b8a0-e2dbbfd4ca94" facs="#m-820addb4-355c-46c8-83f1-3d4676c24344" label="text-like">Compline of Sunday.</l><l xml:id="m-0e1e95e8-e684-48b0-80ab-238ba256e135" facs="#m-128b8f2d-4faa-4412-9776-b45fba4f32c9" label="text-like">At Prime. Ant. Quem vidistis. D. 395. Psalms as on Feasts. In the</l><l xml:id="m-82f2573d-6645-442d-a5ef-22913fee3179" facs="#m-27eaf6b0-e44e-4b0a-924e-21ca533e0e99" label="lyrics-like">Short Resp.. V. Qui nátus es. .  Short Lesson Itaque. p. 436.</l><l xml:id="m-e5f60e46-99a9-4aac-913e-f2ee6dc411a8" facs="#m-c22638db-abfc-45d2-bc57-494f64687cfb" label="text-like">AT TERCE.</l><l xml:id="m-02c98647-0e93-414f-b47b-ff4db2789aa3" facs="#m-197c87ce-3ba6-46ed-aba4-bd2ff3b37ec3" label="lyrics-like">Ant. Génuit puérpera Régem. p. 396. Chapter from Vespers. Fratres:</l><l xml:id="m-a4280ad9-529b-4548-add1-3f1cb0dab26a" facs="#m-beb4837f-01d9-4e1d-a259-a7a70c55b298" label="lyrics-like">Quanto témpore. D. 437. Short Resp. Vérbum cáro. V. Ipse invocábit</l><l xml:id="m-86734a11-64fe-4fa8-b8f1-f22b8bad7522" facs="#m-27e60d33-f3d6-4951-b03a-704f62414a4b" label="text-like">me. as on the Feasi of the Nattvity, p. 407.</l><l xml:id="m-0da72549-0369-4533-aa61-163d186593fb" facs="#m-709cf446-b01e-4889-944c-7f6bd5f37ee5" label="text-like">AT MASS.</l><l xml:id="m-dfd00020-be8f-4f0e-ab7b-20133620f749" facs="#m-ff2d15ec-7d48-4805-93d9-869bb0ffcc2e" label="ambiguous">Intr.</l><l xml:id="m-7df71779-c138-4cb1-8c41-188b5fab2ea9" facs="#m-73c60058-c7ba-4672-9cd5-9717f75da555" label="ambiguous">s.</l><l xml:id="m-7aed9de5-6433-4699-bd4b-e829adadc0e2" facs="#m-43805a1a-b80d-464a-abf7-d3435eedf0e6" label="ambiguo